<title>FRANCE: Elf says sold Suez stake to Electrafina.</title>
<headline>Elf says sold Suez stake to Electrafina.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-10-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>French oil company Elf Aquitaine said on Monday it had sold its entire 2.9 percent stake in Cie Financiere de Suez to Belgium's Electrafina this morning on the Paris Bourse.</p>
<p>Electrafina is a unit of Groupe Bruxelles Lambert (GBL).  </p>
<p>On Thursday, Elf sold its entire 7.06 percent stake, or 1,787,793 shares, in Belgium's Compagnie Nationale a Portefeuille (CNP) to Fibelpar.</p>
<p>CNP is an investment vehicle of Albert Frere, who controls Groupe Bruxelles Lambert.</p>
<p>Since the start of the year Elf has its stakes in Belgian refiner Petrofina, French conglomerate Compagnie Generale des Eaux and CNP.</p>
<p>Electrafina said in Brussels it was paying six billion Belgian francs for the Suez stake.</p>
</text>
